# The crossing for a row three blocks deep: the crossing tile turned a quarter,
# north-south flat at y = 1 down the middle column, west-east climbing over it
# along the middle row (whose comments say why the stones keep the two apart).
# The flat arm is three blocks, port, centre, port, so a repeater in it sits at
# the centre under the bridge; the climbing arm has no room for one, and the
# tile cannot be turned to give it one (that takes five blocks of depth).
tile cross_s
size 5 4 3
port W io 0 1 1
port E io 4 1 1
port N io 2 1 0
port S io 2 1 2
function cross

legend
  G minecraft:glass
  # minecraft:stone
  - minecraft:redstone_wire

layer 0
  ..G..
  G.G.G
  ..G..
layer 1
  ..-..
  -#-#-
  ..-..
layer 2
  .....
  .-#-.
  .....
layer 3
  .....
  ..-..
  .....
